INT. MERCY GENERAL - NIGHT SHIFT NURSES' STATION - NIGHT

Open-plan. Too many monitors. A drooping fern and a laminated sign: PLEASE DON'T MICROWAVE FISH.

KOFI (30s, scrubs, headset) taps at a laptop with a video call open. TARA (20s, lanyard bursting with pins) wheels over on a stool and PIP (intern, 22) hovers behind her with a clipboard held like a shield, while a janitor mops slowly in the background and a drip pole in the corner, for no reason, slowly rotates by itself.

On Kofi's screen: a Slack channel, #night-shift-chaos.

ON SCREEN: ORRIN: has anyone seen the thing in room 6

ON SCREEN: ORRIN: the glowing thing

KOFI
Orrin's on his break and he's already losing it.

TARA
Orrin's always losing it. Last week he said the fridge was talking.

KOFI
The fridge was talking. That was the fridge's night-shift voice.

On the laptop, DR. NAKAMURA's face fills a Zoom window, pixelated, ceiling fan behind him.

DR. NAKAMURA (V.O.)
(over video)
Team, can you hear me? Admissions says there's a patient in six who isn't on the board.

PIP
Is that bad?

DR. NAKAMURA (V.O.)
It's a patient who isn't on the board.

TARA
So, yes.

THE WOMAN (60s, nightgown, barefoot, faintly luminous) steps out of the corridor and stands at the end of the desk, perfectly calm.

PIP
Ma'am? Are you looking for someone?

THE WOMAN
Good evening. I'm told this is where the others wait.

Kofi shuts the laptop lid, hard. Dr. Nakamura's voice is cut off mid-word.

KOFI
Others?

THE WOMAN
My name is Elspeth. I was admitted four hundred years ago. Is there still a form?

Silence. The mop stops. The drip pole stops.

ON SCREEN (Kofi's phone, face up): ORRIN: told u

TARA
(very quiet)
Kofi, get the clipboard.

ELSPETH smiles, patient, and holds out her hand.
